mentsOfLongTermDebt" scale="6" id="f-2985">70</ix:nonFraction> was repaid. Accordingly, there are <ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-682" decimals="INF" name="us-gaap:SecuredDebt" format="ixt:fixed-zero" scale="0" id="f-2986">no</ix:nonFraction> borrowings secured by finance receivables that are outstanding as of December&#160;31, 2025.</span></div><div style="margin-top:5pt"><span style="color:#da2031;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Interest</span></div><div style="margin-top:5pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Interest paid on our short-term and long-term debt amounted to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-1" decimals="-6" name="us-gaap:InterestPaid" scale="6" id="f-2987">272</ix:nonFraction>, $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-12" decimals="-6" name="us-gaap:InterestPaid" scale="6" id="f-2988">214</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-19" decimals="-6" name="us-gaap:InterestPaid" scale="6" id="f-2989">201</ix:nonFraction> for the years ended December&#160;31, 2025, 2024 and 2023, respectively. <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="c-1" name="us-gaap:InterestIncomeAndInterestExpenseDisclosureTableTextBlock" id="f-2990" continuedAt="f-2990-1" escape="true">Interest expense and interest income was as follows: </ix:nonNumeric></span></div><ix:continuation id="f-2990-1"><div style="margin-top:5pt;text-align:justify"><table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"><tr><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:52.116%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.384%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:13.812%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.530%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:13.812%"/><